03/09/2026: Worked with Robert to calculate the air flow of the 4.5V DC motor from Adafruit. We used volume displacement in order to calculate the air flow - we blew the 4.5V motor into a plastic ziploc bag for 30s,
and kept the ziploc bag sealed. We then placed the ziploc bag full of air in a tub full to the brim of water, and measured how much water was left after the bag of air pushed out water. Using the density of water,
1g/ml, we could calculate the LPM using the equation: (water displaced [g])/(0.5 [min])/(1000 [l/g]). Using this equation, we found the air flow rate of the 4.5V Adafruit DC motor to be about 2.5 Liters per Minute.
